    cuda: extend transport telemetry with D2H and CUDA-split counts
    
    The host-to-device counters alone did not explain why decode with
    host-resident KV cannot overlap. Counting device-to-host copies and
    CUDA graph_compute invocations does: at depth 32,768 a decode token
    carries 33 CUDA splits and 32 device-to-host copies totalling 2.2 MB.
    The bytes are negligible; each copy is what matters, because the
    scheduler has no async path for a CUDA source into a CPU destination and
    drains the GPU on every one of them.
    
    That is the store side of the cache -- new rows are quantized on the
    accelerator, pulled back, and written into the host body by a CPU
    set_rows -- and it is what caps read-side overlap at zero.
    
    Still opt-in through GGML_KV_TRANSPORT_STATS and still untouched when
    unset.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E8bBMKTLSzVbDBSUfdQc9N

